Usage: top [options]
  -b, --batch        Batch mode
  -c, --command      Show command line instead of process name
  -d, --delay DELAY  Update interval (default: 3s)
  -H, --threads      Show threads as if they were processes
  -n, --iterations N Exit after N iterations
  -o, --field-sort F Sort by CPU|MEM|TIME|PID|NAME
  -p, --pid PIDS     Monitor only comma-separated PIDs
  -s, --secure-mode  Secure mode (disables kill/renice)
  -u, --user USER    Monitor only processes with given user
  -U, --User USER    Monitor only by real user ID/name
  -w, --width WIDTH  Override output width
      --rows N       Limit number of displayed processes
      --help         Show help
  -v, --version      Show version

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.